# Build-time config for the PWA. These are CLIENT values — they ship inside the
# public JS bundle by design and are safe to commit:
#   - the Supabase anon key is RLS-protected (Supabase docs explicitly say it is
#     safe to expose in client code)
#   - the URLs are public endpoints
# Committing them lets `npm run build` work anywhere (CI, a cloud agent, a fresh
# clone) with no secret plumbing. Rotate via the Supabase / Cloudflare dashboards
# if ever needed. Local dev can still override these in web/.env.local.
